{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating motion commands (controllable) from sensor events (uncontrollable). The specification enforces conservative obstacle recovery, ensures forward progress when clear, and prevents unsafe actions after obstacle events. Recovery states use rotate or backward actions as appropriate, with full_rotate reserved for repeated blockages. All uncontrollable events are handled in every state, and only one controllable is enabled per state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception, unified into a single plant for simplicity.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-oriented exploration with conservative recovery and minimal helper states."
